Directory Module
Updated Developer Description and Data Structure

Purpose. The Directory Module is a centralized, searchable contact directory organized by barangay and contact
type. It allows authorized staff to maintain contact records and view aggregate directory counts by barangay.
1. Directory Data Entry
Field Description
Barangay Select the barangay associated with the contact.
Type of Contact Sectoral, Barangay Officials, Neighborhood Association, Coordinator, Leader, Supporter, Others.
Name Full name of the contact.
Position Position, designation, role, or title.
Contact Number Primary contact/mobile number.
Other Info Additional relevant notes or directory information.
Internal Label Saint, Sinner, or Savable. User-defined internal category.
2. Internal Label Display
The module may include three user-defined internal directory labels. These labels are stored as administrative
categories without the system assigning a political meaning or persuasion score.
Label Display Color System Description
Saint Blue User-defined internal directory category.
Sinner Green User-defined internal directory category.
Savable Yellow User-defined internal directory category.
3. Barangay Directory Summary
When a barangay is clicked, the dashboard should show the total number of directory records and the breakdown by
contact type. It may also display aggregate counts of records carrying each internal label.
Summary Metric Example
Total Contacts 207
Saint label count 95
Sinner label count 62
Savable label count 50
Sectoral 18
Barangay Officials 12
Neighborhood Associations 9
Coordinators 15

Leaders 25
Supporters 120
Others 8
4. Search and Filtering
The directory should be searchable by Name, Position, Contact Type, and Barangay. Authorized staff can filter by
contact type. Individual records can be opened for viewing or updating.
5. Map Behavior
When Directory is selected, the Mariveles barangay map remains interactive. Clicking a barangay opens its directory
summary and contact list. The map visualization should use neutral operational measures such as total directory
records, contact-type distribution, or directory completeness, rather than automatically interpreting the internal
labels as political support or targeting signals.
6. Core Data Logic
Barangay -> Type of Contact -> Name -> Position -> Contact Number -> Other Info -> Internal Label
The dashboard can automatically generate Total Contacts per Barangay + Breakdown by Contact Type +
Aggregate Internal Label Counts + Searchable Directory.
7. Privacy and Access
Because the directory contains names, contact numbers, notes, and internal labels, access should be restricted to
authorized staff. The system should maintain an audit trail showing who created or edited a record and should not
expose personal contact information or internal labels on a public-facing dashboard.